            <ArticleTitle>Gene therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>416-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gene therapy is not yet possible, but may become feasible soon, particularly for well understood gene defects. Although treatment of a patient raises no ethical problems once it can be done well, changing the genes of an early embryo is more difficult, controversial and unlikely to be required clinically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
